  "notes": "High-pressure nonmagnetic Pnma Fe3C. The measured structural cell is Prescher (2012) Table S1 at 47.4 GPa and 293 K, cyclically transformed to standard Pnma axes, without rescaling. Full occupancies express ideal Fe3C stoichiometry, not refined occupancies. Takahashi (2019) thermal EOS V0 values are extrapolated 300 K zero-pressure intercepts and differ from this finite-pressure structural volume. Two pressure scales describe the same experiment. Source-equation benchmarks pass, while conditional P/V/T-coordinate-width refits achieve central-coefficient parity; KBr errors reproduce printed precision while MgO errors do not, and exact source weights and selection remain unconfirmed; no author-workflow reproduction or independent experimental validation is claimed.",
